---
permalink: /ui_kits/website/weddings.html
title: Weddings & Banns of Marriage
subtitle: We love weddings — and are always delighted to pray for and accompany
  couples as they take this important step.
intro_content: >-
  If you are engaged and considering getting married at Emmanuel or St
  Cuthbert's, we would love to hear from you!


  We love weddings and are always delighted to pray for and accompany couples as
  they take this important step. We warmly encourage couples to attend three or
  four marriage preparation sessions ahead of the wedding day; these will be
  arranged between the priest and the couple, and will ensure that sessions are
  compatible with work and other commitments.


  **Marriage, Civil Partnership and Weddings for same sex couples<br />**Whilst
  we’re not yet able to marry same-sex couples in the Church of England, at
  Emmanuel we are pleased to offer services for same-sex couples who have
  recently celebrated a wedding or civil partnership. We are members of
  Inclusive Church and have a proud tradition of LGBTQIA+ welcome and inclusion.
  We would be happy to accompany you and pray with you as you mark a new stage
  in your relationship.


  If you would like to know more about weddings in either of our churches,
  please [contact the parish office](contact.html) in the first instance and a
  member of the clergy will be in touch.
wedding_images:
  - image: /assets/cms/site-images/weddings-1.jpg
    image_alt: A bride and groom standing together at the altar during their wedding
      ceremony, surrounded by candles and flowers
  - image: /assets/cms/site-images/weddings-2.jpg
    image_alt: A newly married couple sharing a joyful moment in the church after
      their wedding
  - image: /assets/uploads/j-p-wedding-church-steps.jpeg
    image_alt: ''
  - image: /assets/uploads/jonathan-priyanka-trin.jpeg
    image_alt: ''
callout:
  - heading: Let's begin the conversation.
    body: Tell us a little about you and your plans, and a member of the clergy will
      be in touch to talk through the next steps.
    primary_button:
      - label: Contact the parish office
        href: contact.html
    secondary_button:
      - label: About the electoral roll
        href: electoral-roll.html
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<title>{{ title }} — Emmanuel Church, West Hampstead</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
<style>
  .em-faq__q {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .em-faq .em-ornament { margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .em-faq h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-h2);
    font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
    color: var(--navy);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    line-height: 1.04;
    margin: 0;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .em-faq-body { padding-top: 22px; }
  .em-intro--solo .inner { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .wedding-photo-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 24px; }
  .wedding-photo-row .em-well { height: 280px; }
  @media (max-width: 1024px) { .wedding-photo-row { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .wedding-photo-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .em-pagehead .meta-row { flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
    .em-intro .inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; gap: 32px; }
    .em-faq h2 { font-size: 26px; }
    .wedding-photo-row { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr) !important; gap: 8px; margin-top: 20px; }
    .wedding-photo-row .em-well { height: 140px; }
    .em-aside { position: static; }
  }
</style>
<link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/assets/favicon.ico" />
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/assets/favicon-32.png" />
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/assets/apple-touch-icon.png" />
</head>
<body>

{% include "header.njk" %}

  <section class="em-pagehead em-pagehead--band">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="em-breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><a href="baptisms.html">Life Events</a><span class="sep">/</span><span>Weddings & Banns of Marriage</span></div>
      <h1 data-editable="text" data-prop="title" data-type="span">{{ title }}</h1>
      <p class="deck" data-editable="text" data-prop="subtitle" data-type="text">{{ subtitle }}</p>
      <div class="meta-row"><div class="item"><div class="k">Where</div><div class="v">Emmanuel or St Cuthbert's</div></div><div class="item"><div class="k">Preparation</div><div class="v">3–4 sessions</div></div><div class="item"><div class="k">First step</div><div class="v">Contact the parish office</div></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="em-intro em-intro--solo">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="em-body">
        <div data-editable="text" data-prop="intro_content" data-type="html">
          {% for para in intro_content.split("\n\n") %}<p>{{ para | trim | safe }}</p>{% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="wedding-photo-row" style="margin-top:36px" data-editable="array" data-prop="wedding_images">
        {% for photo in wedding_images %}
          <div class="em-well" data-editable="array-item"><img src="{{ photo.image }}" alt="{{ photo.image_alt }}" /></div>
        {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="em-faq" style="margin-top:36px">
          <div class="em-ornament is-leading">A common question</div>
          <div class="em-faq__q">
            <h2>Can I get married at Emmanuel?</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="em-faq-body">
            <p class="em-lead" style="font-style:normal;font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:18px;color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.6">If you live in the parish, it is very straightforward. If you don't, we need to establish whether you have a qualifying connection — you only need <em>one</em> of the following:</p>
            <ul class="em-checklist">
              <li>You and/or your fiancé(e) are on the electoral roll of Emmanuel or St Cuthbert's.</li>
              <li>One or both of you were baptised in the parish (by a Church of England service).</li>
              <li>One or both of you have been confirmed (by a Church of England service), with the confirmation entered in a register belonging to a church in the parish.</li>
              <li>One or both of you have parents or grandparents who were married in the parish by a Church of England service.</li>
              <li>One or both of you have had your usual place of residence in the parish for at least 6 months.</li>
              <li>One or both of your parents had their usual place of residence in the parish for at least 6 months during your lifetime.</li>
              <li>One or both of you have habitually attended public worship at Church of England services in the parish for at least 6 months.</li>
              <li>One or both of your parents have habitually attended public worship at Church of England services in the parish for at least 6 months during your lifetime.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% for c in callout %}
  <section class="em-callout">
    <div class="inner">
      <div>
        <h3 data-editable="text" data-prop="heading" data-type="span">{{ c.heading }}</h3>
        <p data-editable="text" data-prop="body" data-type="text">{{ c.body }}</p>
      </div>
      {% if (c.primary_button and c.primary_button.length) or (c.secondary_button and c.secondary_button.length) %}
      <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        {% for btn in c.primary_button %}<a href="{{ btn.href }}" {% if btn.href | isexternal %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %} class="em-btn em-btn--tan">{{ btn.label }}</a>{% endfor %}
        {% for btn in c.secondary_button %}<a href="{{ btn.href }}" {% if btn.href | isexternal %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %} class="em-btn em-btn--ghost-light">{{ btn.label }}</a>{% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

{% include "footer.njk" %}

</body>
</html>
